    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A 22-year-old male presents to the office with a 5-day history of diarrhea after completing his third course of antibiotics for mastoiditis. Physical examination reveals vague generalized abdominal pain on palpation. Culture on hektoen enteric agar is positive. The most likely etiologic agent causing the diarrhea is\n\nOptions: \nA. Clostridium difficile\nB. Entamoeba histolytica\nC. Vibrio cholerae\nD. Escherichia coli\nE. Staphylococcus aureus\nF. Campylobacter jejuni\nG. Giardia lamblia\nH. Salmonella typhi\nI. Yersinia enterocolitica\nJ. Shigella dysenteriae\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
