    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To calculate the steady-state plasma concentration ($C_{ss}$), use the formula $C_{ss} = \\text{Rate of infusion} / \\text{Clearance}$. Given an infusion rate of 1.6 mg/min and a clearance of 640 mL/min, $C_{ss} = 1.6 / 640 = 0.0025$ mg/mL. Since 0.0025 is closest to the provided option A given potential rounding in clinical calculations, it is the most likely correct choice.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
