    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{I}. While several presidents in the list engaged in Latin American politics, John F. Kennedy is widely recognized for his significant policy intervention in the region, most notably the establishment of the Alliance for Progress in 1961. This initiative was a major attempt to promote economic development and democratic reform in Latin America during the twentieth century.",
