      "generated_answer": "The Bandung Conference of 1955 was a pivotal gathering where leaders from newly independent nations discussed non-alignment to avoid being forced to choose sides between the United States and the Soviet Union. Sukarno and other leaders sought to create a \"Third World\" bloc that would remain independent of the global power struggle inherent in the Cold War. Therefore, their neutral stance was specifically aimed at navigating the geopolitical tensions between the two superpowers.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
