    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The most likely correct answer is \\boxed{D}.\n\nFrederick Douglass was a prominent social reformer and orator who dedicated his life to the struggle for the emancipation of enslaved people. As a leading figure and former enslaved person, his rhetoric and advocacy were central to the Abolitionist Movement, which sought the immediate end of slavery in the United States.",
