      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{B}. \n\nThe \"obstetrical dilemma\" theory posits that human infants must be born in a relatively undeveloped state because the evolution of bipedalism narrowed the birth canal, while the evolution of larger brains necessitated a smaller fetal head size at birth. Consequently, the brain undergoes most of its rapid growth after birth, which is the definition of the secondarily altricial condition.",
