    "global index": "MMLUPro_history_4548",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This question refers to the following information.\n\"The seeds of totalitarian regimes are nurtured by misery and want. They spread and grow in the evil soil of poverty and strife. They reach their full growth when the hope of a people for a better life has died. We must keep that hope alive. . . . Great responsibilities have been placed upon us by the swift movement of events. . . . I am confident that the Congress will face these responsibilities squarely.\"\n—President Harry S. Truman, 1947\nThe passage above is part of President Truman's argument to Congress in favor of\n\nOptions: \nA. the Servicemen's Readjustment Act (G.I. Bill).\nB. an extension of aid to Greece and Turkey.\nC. desegregation of the U.S. armed forces\nD. the Taft-Hartley Act\nE. the McCarran Internal Security Act.\nF. the Marshall Plan for European recovery\nG. development of the hydrogen bomb.\nH. the implementation of the Fair Deal\nI. the creation of the United Nations\nJ. establishment of NATO\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "This passage is taken from the Truman Doctrine speech delivered on March 12, 1947, in which President Truman requested congressional funds to support Greece and Turkey against the threat of communist expansion. By framing the aid as a necessity to combat the \"misery and want\" that nurtures totalitarianism, he established the policy of containment. Therefore, the argument serves as the justification for providing financial and military assistance to those two nations.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
