    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The markings found on the mud-bricks of Huaca del Sol are interpreted by archaeologists as \"maker's marks,\" which served to identify the specific social groups or communities responsible for producing those bricks as part of a mita-style labor system. By attributing batches of bricks to specific groups, the site administrators could track and organize the massive labor contributions required for the construction. Therefore, the most likely correct answer is C.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
      "success": true,
