      "generated_answer": "The most likely correct answer is \\boxed{A}.\n\nWhile the Cold War and other external pressures played a role in African history, the primary obstacle to Nkrumah’s vision of a unified \"United States of Africa\" was the immense diversity of the continent’s ethnic, linguistic, and cultural groups. These deep-seated disparities, often exacerbated by colonial-era borders, made the creation of a singular, cohesive political union extremely difficult to achieve.",
