    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the evidence for trade between Indus Valley cities and the city states of ancient Mesopotamia?\n\nOptions: \nA. Mesopotamian cuneiform tablets have been discovered in the Indus Valley.\nB. All of the above.\nC. Harappan coins have been found in Mesopotamia, and Mesopotamian coins have been found in the Indus Valley.\nD. Obsidian tools have been found at sites in both regions.\nE. Harappan seals have been found in Mesopotamia and Mesopotamian cylinder seals have been found in the Indus valley.\nF. Pottery styles similar to those found in Mesopotamia have been discovered in the Indus Valley.\nG. Archaeological evidence shows that there was no trade between the two regions.\nH. Stone axes from the Indus Valley have been found in Mesopotamia.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
