      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{J}. \n\nIn the *Dred Scott v. Sandford* decision, Chief Justice Roger Taney ruled that Congress lacked the authority to prohibit slavery in the territories, effectively declaring the Missouri Compromise unconstitutional. This aligns with Frederick Douglass's characterization of the Federal Government being pledged to support and protect the institution of slavery.",
