      "generated_answer": "The most likely correct answer is \\boxed{D}.\n\nArticle 1 of Source 1 expresses the expectation that the union of Venezuela and New Granada into a single republic would create a powerful and prosperous nation. Sectionalism among local elites—who often prioritized regional interests and power over a centralized national government—directly challenged this unity and eventually led to the collapse of Gran Colombia. Other options, while historical factors, were either strengthening forces or less central to the specific internal disintegration of the unified project described in Source 1.",
