      "generated_answer": "The first passage from the Qur'an condemns strong drink, gambling, and idols as \"an infamy of Satan's handiwork\" and urges believers to avoid them for success, indicating a moral and religious prohibition rooted in divine command. This aligns most closely with a strict, moralistic religious tone that discourages worldly pleasures. \n\n\\boxed{I}",
