    "global index": "MMLUPro_history_4759",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This question refers to the following information.\n\"The struggle against neo-colonialism is not aimed at excluding the capital of the developed world from operating in less developed countries. It is aimed at preventing the financial power of the developed countries being used in such a way as to impoverish the less developed.\nNon-alignment, as practiced by Ghana and many other countries, is based on co-operation with all States whether they be capitalist, socialist or have a mixed economy. Such a policy, therefore, involves foreign investment from capitalist countries, but it must be invested in accordance with a national plan drawn up by the government of the non-aligned State with its own interests in mind. The issue is not what return the foreign investor receives on his investments…The question is one of power. A State in the grip of neo-colonialism is not master of its own destiny.\"\nKwame Nkrumah, Neo-Colonialism, 1965\nWhich of the following is referenced by the co-operation mentioned in the second paragraph?\n\nOptions: \nA. The competing ideologies of World War II\nB. The competing colonization companies in the Scramble for Africa\nC. The competing empires of World War I\nD. The competing blocs during the Korean War\nE. The competing empires during the Crusades\nF. The competing ideologies of the Cold War\nG. The competing powers during the Industrial Revolution\nH. The competing nations during the Cuban Missile Crisis\nI. The competing political systems during the French Revolution\nJ. The competing alliances during the Napoleonic Wars\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The passage discusses \"non-alignment,\" a foreign policy strategy adopted by many newly independent nations during the mid-20th century to remain neutral between the two dominant global superpowers. This non-aligned movement was specifically a response to the ideological conflict between the capitalist United States and the socialist Soviet Union. Therefore, the \"co-operation with all States whether they be capitalist, socialist or have a mixed economy\" refers to the Cold War.\n\n\\boxed{F}",
      "success": true,
