      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{G}.\n\nSacagawea acted as a vital guide and interpreter for the Lewis and Clark Expedition, just as Samoset and Squanto provided essential linguistic and geographical assistance to the Plymouth colonists. Both represent indigenous figures who facilitated communication and navigation between Native American groups and early European explorers or settlers.",
