      "generated_answer": "The boycott mentioned in the excerpt refers to the Swadeshi (boycott of foreign cloth) movement promoted by Gandhi during the Non-Cooperation Movement. The aftermath of World War I provided the economic instability, nationalist fervor, and colonial disillusionment necessary to mobilize the Indian public against British-manufactured goods. This context directly empowered the promotion of indigenous cloth production (khadi) as both an economic and political weapon.\n\n\\boxed{F}",
