      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{F}.\n\nBy observing that moons revolve around Jupiter, Galileo provided empirical evidence that not all celestial bodies orbit the Earth. This challenged the prevailing geocentric model of the universe and laid the groundwork for the acceptance of a heliocentric system where the Earth is not the center. Options like G are observations rather than revolutionary conclusions, while others are factually incorrect or secondary in historical impact.",
