      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    # Read input from stdin\n    input_data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not input_data:\n        return\n    \n    n = int(input_data[0])\n    m = int(input_data[1])\n    s = input_data[2]\n    \n    # We want to find the minimum number of logo T-shirts (let's say K)\n    # such that we can satisfy the requirements.\n    # The total number of T-shirts available is M (plain) + K (logo).\n    # Since plain T-shirts can only be used for meals (1), and logo T-shirts\n    # can be used for both meals (1) and programming (2), we simulate the process\n    # for a given K.\n    \n    def check(k):\n        plain_available = m\n        logo_available = k\n        \n        for char in s:\n            if char == '0':\n                # Wash day: replenish all sets\n                plain_available = m\n                logo_available = k\n            elif char == '1':\n                # Meal: prefer plain, then logo\n                if plain_available > 0:\n                    plain_available -= 1\n                elif logo_available > 0:\n                    logo_available -= 1\n                else:\n                    return False\n            elif char == '2':\n                # Competitive programming: must use logo\n                if logo_available > 0:\n                    logo_available -= 1\n                else:\n                    return False\n        return True\n\n    # Binary search for the minimum K\n    # Min K is 0, Max K is N\n    low = 0\n    high = n\n    ans = n\n    \n    while low <= high:\n        mid = (low + high) // 2\n        if check(mid):\n            ans = mid\n            high = mid - 1\n        else:\n            low = mid + 1\n            \n    print(ans)\n\n# Execute the function\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    solve()\n```",
