    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To solve this problem, we use a Disjoint Set Union (DSU) to maintain the connected components of the graph. \n\nTwo vertices $x_i$ and $y_i$ become connected in $G^{(i)}$ if the added edge $(p_i, q_i)$ bridges the existing components containing $x_i$ and $y_i$. Specifically, adding $(p_i, q_i)$ makes $x_i$ and $y_i$ reachable if and only if one of them is in the same component as $p_i$ and the other is in the same component as $q_i$ (or vice versa). \n\nWe map each vertex to its DSU component representative. For each prohibited pair $(x_i, y_i)$, we store the requirement that their component representatives $(root(x_i), root(y_i))$ must **not** be joined.\n\n```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    input_data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not input_data:\n        return\n    \n    idx = 0\n    N = int(input_data[idx]); idx += 1\n    M = int(input_data[idx]); idx += 1\n    \n    parent = list(range(N + 1))\n    def find(i):\n        if parent[i] == i:\n            return i\n        parent[i] = find(parent[i])\n        return parent[i]\n\n    def union(i, j):\n        root_i = find(i)\n        root_j = find(j)\n        if root_i != root_j:\n            parent[root_i] = root_j\n\n    for _ in range(M):\n        u = int(input_data[idx]); idx += 1\n        v = int(input_data[idx]); idx += 1\n        union(u, v)\n\n    K = int(input_data[idx]); idx += 1\n    bad_pairs = set()\n    for _ in range(K):\n        x = int(input_data[idx]); idx += 1\n        y = int(input_data[idx]); idx += 1\n        rx, ry = find(x), find(y)\n        if rx > ry: rx, ry = ry, rx\n        bad_pairs.add((rx, ry))\n\n    Q = int(input_data[idx]); idx += 1\n    results = []\n    for _ in range(Q):\n        p = int(input_data[idx]); idx += 1\n        q = int(input_data[idx]); idx += 1\n        rp, rq = find(p), find(q)\n        \n        if rp == rq:\n            # Adding edge within same component doesn't connect any *new* components\n            results.append(\"Yes\")\n        else:\n            # Edge connects two components. Check if any bad pair spans these.\n            # We need all forbidden pairs (rx, ry) to NOT have one root in {rp, rq} \n            # and the other in the other set.\n            # Effectively: check if any bad pair connects the components now being merged.\n            # This is equivalent to checking if the new edge triggers a prohibited path.\n            if rp > rq: rp, rq = rq, rp\n            \n            # The edge connects component rp and component rq.\n            # A pair (rx, ry) becomes connected if {rx, ry} == {rp, rq}\n            if (rp, rq) in bad_pairs:\n                results.append(\"No\")\n            else:\n                results.append(\"Yes\")\n                \n    sys.stdout.write(\"\\n\".join(results) + \"\\n\")\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    # Increase recursion depth for deep DSU trees\n    sys.setrecursionlimit(300000)\n    solve()\n```",
