      "generated_answer": "To solve this problem efficiently, we recognize that adding edges between every pair of vertices in a set $S_i$ with weight $C_i$ is equivalent to connecting every vertex in $S_i$ to a virtual node with weight $C_i / 2$. A more practical approach for Kruskal's algorithm without creating a complete graph (which would have $O(K_i^2)$ edges) is to connect the vertices in $S_i$ sequentially in a line (or chain) using edges of weight $C_i$.\n\nSince we need a Minimum Spanning Tree (MST), we collect all potential edges: for each operation $i$, we connect $A_{i,j}$ and $A_{i,j+1}$ with an edge of weight $C_i$ for all $1 \\le j < K_i$. We sort all these edges by weight and use a Disjoint Set Union (DSU) to build the MST.\n\n```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    # Read N and M\n    input_data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not input_data:\n        return\n    \n    idx = 0\n    N = int(input_data[idx]); idx += 1\n    M = int(input_data[idx]); idx += 1\n    \n    edges = []\n    for _ in range(M):\n        K = int(input_data[idx]); idx += 1\n        C = int(input_data[idx]); idx += 1\n        nodes = []\n        for _ in range(K):\n            nodes.append(int(input_data[idx]))\n            idx += 1\n        \n        # Connect nodes in the set S_i as a chain\n        # This is sufficient to represent the connectivity of the complete graph\n        # formed by weight C_i.\n        for j in range(K - 1):\n            edges.append((C, nodes[j], nodes[j+1]))\n            \n    # Sort edges by weight\n    edges.sort()\n    \n    # Kruskal's Algorithm\n    parent = list(range(N + 1))\n    def find(i):\n        if parent[i] == i:\n            return i\n        parent[i] = find(parent[i])\n        return parent[i]\n    \n    def union(i, j):\n        root_i = find(i)\n        root_j = find(j)\n        if root_i != root_j:\n            parent[root_i] = root_j\n            return True\n        return False\n    \n    mst_weight = 0\n    edges_count = 0\n    for weight, u, v in edges:\n        if union(u, v):\n            mst_weight += weight\n            edges_count += 1\n            \n    if edges_count == N - 1:\n        print(mst_weight)\n    else:\n        print(-1)\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    # Increase recursion depth for deep DSU trees, though iterative path compression is preferred.\n    sys.setrecursionlimit(300000)\n    solve()\n```",
