      "generated_answer": "To solve this problem, we need to calculate the change in the number of green connected components when a specific red cell $(i, j)$ is turned green.\n\nLet $C$ be the initial number of green connected components. When a red cell at $(i, j)$ is turned green, it connects to its $k$ neighboring green cells $(0 \\le k \\le 4)$. If these $k$ neighbors belong to $m$ distinct connected components, the new number of components will be $C - m + 1$. \n\nThe expected value is:\n$\\frac{1}{R} \\sum_{\\text{red cells}} (C - m + 1)$, where $R$ is the total count of red cells.\nTotal sum $= R \\cdot (C + 1) - \\sum_{\\text{red cells}} m$.\n\nWe use a Disjoint Set Union (DSU) or simple component labeling to identify components of existing green cells.\n\n```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    input_data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    H = int(input_data[0])\n    W = int(input_data[1])\n    grid = input_data[2:]\n    \n    MOD = 998244353\n    \n    # Label green components\n    comp = [[0] * W for _ in range(H)]\n    c_id = 0\n    adj = [(-1, 0), (1, 0), (0, -1), (0, 1)]\n    \n    for r in range(H):\n        for c in range(W):\n            if grid[r][c] == '#' and comp[r][c] == 0:\n                c_id += 1\n                stack = [(r, c)]\n                comp[r][c] = c_id\n                while stack:\n                    curr_r, curr_c = stack.pop()\n                    for dr, dc in adj:\n                        nr, nc = curr_r + dr, curr_c + dc\n                        if 0 <= nr < H and 0 <= nc < W and grid[nr][nc] == '#' and comp[nr][nc] == 0:\n                            comp[nr][nc] = c_id\n                            stack.append((nr, nc))\n                            \n    red_cells = []\n    for r in range(H):\n        for c in range(W):\n            if grid[r][c] == '.':\n                red_cells.append((r, c))\n                \n    R = len(red_cells)\n    \n    # Calculate initial components (C)\n    total_change = 0\n    for r, c in red_cells:\n        neighbor_comps = set()\n        for dr, dc in adj:\n            nr, nc = r + dr, c + dc\n            if 0 <= nr < H and 0 <= nc < W and grid[nr][nc] == '#':\n                neighbor_comps.add(comp[nr][nc])\n        # After filling, we lose len(neighbor_comps) existing comps and add 1\n        total_change += (1 - len(neighbor_comps))\n        \n    # Expected value = C + (sum of changes) / R\n    ans = (c_id * R + total_change) % MOD\n    inv_R = pow(R, MOD - 2, MOD)\n    print((ans * inv_R) % MOD)\n\nsolve()\n```",
