    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "I'll solve this step by step.\n\n## Problem Understanding\n\n1. We have `n` boxes with weights `a_i`\n2. For each possible `k` (where `k` divides `n`), we can load boxes into trucks with `k` boxes per truck\n3. The first `k` boxes go to truck 1, next `k` to truck 2, etc.\n4. For each valid `k`, we calculate the maximum absolute difference between any two trucks (which is `max(truck_weights) - min(truck_weights)`)\n5. We need to find the maximum possible such difference across all valid `k`\n\n## Key Insights\n\n1. Valid values of `k` are divisors of `n` (since we need exactly `n/k` trucks, each with `k` boxes)\n2. For each valid `k`, we need to compute the sum of each group of `k` consecutive boxes\n3. The absolute difference for that `k` is `max(group_sums) - min(group_sums)`\n4. We need the maximum of this value across all divisors `k` of `n`\n\n## Algorithm\n\n1. For each test case:\n   - Read `n` and the array `a`\n   - Find all divisors of `n` (these are valid values of `k`)\n   - For each divisor `k`:\n     - Compute the sum of each group: `sum(a[i*k:(i+1)*k])` for `i` from `0` to `n/k - 1`\n     - Find max and min of these sums\n     - Calculate difference = max - min\n   - Return the maximum difference across all divisors\n\nHowever, since the sum of `n` for all test cases ≤ 150,000, we can optimize by using prefix sums to quickly compute group sums.\n\nLet's implement this:\n\n```python\nimport sys\nimport math\n\ndef solve():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    t = int(data[0])\n    index = 1\n    results = []\n    \n    for _ in range(t):\n        n = int(data[index])\n        index += 1\n        a = list(map(int, data[index:index + n]))\n        index += n\n        \n        # Compute prefix sums for O(1) range sum queries\n        prefix = [0] * (n + 1)\n        for i in range(n):\n            prefix[i + 1] = prefix[i] + a[i]\n        \n        # Find all divisors of n (valid k values)\n        divisors = []\n        for k in range(1, int(math.sqrt(n)) + 1):\n            if n % k == 0:\n                divisors.append(k)\n                if k != n // k:\n                    divisors.append(n // k)\n        \n        max_diff = 0  # If only one truck, difference is 0\n        \n        # For each valid k (number of boxes per truck)\n        for k in divisors:\n            num_trucks = n // k\n            if num_trucks == 1:\n                # Only one truck, difference is 0\n                continue\n            \n            # Compute group sums using prefix sums\n            group_sums = []\n            for i in range(num_trucks):\n                start = i * k\n                end = start + k\n                group_sum = prefix[end] - prefix[start]\n                group_sums.append(group_sum)\n            \n            diff = max(group_sums) - min(group_sums)\n            if diff > max_diff:\n                max_diff = diff\n        \n        results.append(str(max_diff))\n    \n    print(\"\\n\".join(results))\n\nsolve()\n```",
