0000000 1000000000 1000000000 1000000000\n\n15\n\n60978 82265 78961 56708 39846 31071 4913 4769 29092 91348 64119 72421 98405 222 14294\n\n8\n\n19957 69913 37531 96991 57838 21008 14207 19198\n\n\n\nSample Output 1:\n\n1\n9\n0\n189114\n112141\n\n\nNote\n\nIn the first case, we should pick two trucks, so the first one will have only the first box, and the second one will have only the second box.\n\nIn the second case, we should pick six trucks, so the maximum will be $10$, the minimum will be $1$, and the answer is $10 - 1 = 9$.\n\nIn the third case, for any possible $k$, the trucks will have the same total weight of boxes, so the answer is $0$.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To solve this problem, we need to iterate through all possible divisors $k$ of $n$. For each $k$, we partition the array into segments of length $k$, calculate the sum of each segment, and find the difference between the maximum and minimum sums. Since the sum of $n$ over all test cases is limited to $150,000$, we can optimize the process by precalculating prefix sums, allowing us to compute segment sums in $O(1)$ time. \n\nHere is the Python implementation:\n\n```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    input_data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not input_data:\n        return\n    \n    idx = 0\n    t = int(input_data[idx])\n    idx += 1\n    \n    results = []\n    for _ in range(t):\n        n = int(input_data[idx])\n        idx += 1\n        a = [int(x) for x in input_data[idx:idx+n]]\n        idx += n\n        \n        # Calculate prefix sums to calculate segment sums in O(1)\n        prefix_sums = [0] * (n + 1)\n        for i in range(n):\n            prefix_sums[i+1] = prefix_sums[i] + a[i]\n            \n        # Find divisors of n\n        divisors = []\n        for i in range(1, int(n**0.5) + 1):\n            if n % i == 0:\n                divisors.append(i)\n                if i*i != n:\n                    divisors.append(n // i)\n        \n        max_diff = 0\n        for k in divisors:\n            # We want to check truck capacities k for every divisor\n            # If n % k == 0 is guaranteed by the divisor logic\n            current_min = float('inf')\n            current_max = float('-inf')\n            \n            for i in range(0, n, k):\n                segment_sum = prefix_sums[i+k] - prefix_sums[i]\n                if segment_sum < current_min:\n                    current_min = segment_sum\n                if segment_sum > current_max:\n                    current_max = segment_sum\n            \n            diff = current_max - current_min\n            if diff > max_diff:\n                max_diff = diff\n                \n        results.append(str(max_diff))\n        \n    sys.stdout.write('\\n'.join(results) + '\\n')\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    solve()\n```",
