      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef minimum_time_to_revert(word: str, k: int) -> int:\n    n = len(word)\n    \n    # Try each possible time t (starting from 1)\n    # After t seconds, we've removed t*k characters from the front\n    # and added t*k characters to the end\n    # The string will be: word[t*k % n :] + word[: t*k % n] if we consider the net effect\n    # But more precisely, after t operations, the string becomes:\n    # word[t*k :] + (some k*t characters we added)\n    # For the string to revert to original, the remaining part word[t*k:] must equal the prefix word[:n - t*k]\n    # and the added part must make up for the missing part at the end.\n    # Actually, the string after t seconds will have the form: word[t*k:] + X, where X is any string of length t*k\n    # For this to equal the original word, we need word[t*k:] to equal word[:n - t*k]\n    # and X to equal word[n - t*k:]\n    \n    # But since we can choose X arbitrarily, the only constraint is that word[t*k:] must equal word[:n - t*k]\n    # (so that we can choose X to be exactly word[n - t*k:] and get back the original string)\n    \n    # However, note that if t*k >= n, then after t*k // n full rotations, we have t*k % n characters removed\n    # So effectively, after t seconds, the string is word[t*k % n:] + (some t*k characters)\n    # For the string to match the original, we need word[t*k % n:] == word[:n - t*k % n]\n    \n    # Let's check for each t starting from 1\n    for t in range(1, n + 1):  # t cannot exceed n because eventually we'll cycle\n        suffix_length = n - (t * k) % n\n        if suffix_length == 0:\n            return t  # After t seconds, we've removed exactly n characters (full rotation), so we can add back the same string\n        \n        # Check if word[0:suffix_length] == word[(t*k) % n : (t*k) % n + suffix_length]\n        if word[:suffix_length] == word[(t * k) % n : (t * k) % n + suffix_length]:\n            return t\n    \n    return n  # Fallback (though the loop should always find a solution)\n```",
