    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef numberOfWays(n, x):\n    MOD = 10**9 + 7\n    \n    # Generate all possible x-th powers that are <= n\n    powers = []\n    i = 1\n    while i**x <= n:\n        powers.append(i**x)\n        i += 1\n    \n    # dp[i] represents the number of ways to form sum i\n    dp = [0] * (n + 1)\n    dp[0] = 1  # One way to make sum 0: use no numbers\n    \n    # For each power, update dp array (knapsack style)\n    for power in powers:\n        # Traverse backwards to avoid using the same power multiple times\n        for j in range(n, power - 1, -1):\n            dp[j] = (dp[j] + dp[j - power]) % MOD\n    \n    return dp[n]\n```",
