    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To solve this problem, we first sort the array `nums` to easily calculate the differences between elements. After sorting, any subsequence of length `k` with a power of at least `x` implies that all consecutive elements in the selected subsequence must have a difference of at least `x`.\n\nWe can use dynamic programming: `dp[i][j][last_idx]` representing the number of subsequences of length `j` ending at index `last_idx` with a minimum difference of at least `i`. However, given the constraints ($n \\le 50$), we can use the property that the sum of powers is equal to $\\sum_{x=1}^{\\max\\_diff} P(power \\ge x)$, where $P(power \\ge x)$ is the number of subsequences of length $k$ with a minimum difference of at least $x$.\n\n```python\ndef solve(nums, k):\n    nums.sort()\n    n = len(nums)\n    MOD = 10**9 + 7\n    \n    # helper to count subsequences with min difference >= x\n    def count_with_min_diff(x):\n        # dp[count][last_idx] = number of subsequences of length 'count' \n        # ending at index 'last_idx' with min diff >= x\n        dp = [[0] * n for _ in range(k + 1)]\n        for i in range(n):\n            dp[1][i] = 1\n            \n        for length in range(2, k + 1):\n            for curr in range(n):\n                for prev in range(curr):\n                    if nums[curr] - nums[prev] >= x:\n                        dp[length][curr] = (dp[length][curr] + dp[length - 1][prev]) % MOD\n        \n        return sum(dp[k]) % MOD\n\n    # The max possible difference is the range of nums\n    max_val = nums[-1] - nums[0]\n    total_sum = 0\n    \n    # The sum of powers is sum_{x=1}^{max_val} (count_with_min_diff(x))\n    # We only need to check x up to (nums[-1] - nums[0]) // (k - 1)\n    limit = (nums[-1] - nums[0]) // (k - 1) if k > 1 else max_val\n    for x in range(1, limit + 1):\n        total_sum = (total_sum + count_with_min_diff(x)) % MOD\n        \n    return total_sum\n```",
