      "generated_answer": "```python\nfrom typing import List\nfrom math import gcd\nfrom collections import defaultdict\n\ndef can_traverse_all_pairs(nums: List[int]) -> bool:\n    n = len(nums)\n    if n == 1:\n        return True\n    \n    # Union-Find data structure\n    parent = list(range(n))\n    rank = [0] * n\n    \n    def find(x):\n        if parent[x] != x:\n            parent[x] = find(parent[x])\n        return parent[x]\n    \n    def union(x, y):\n        px, py = find(x), find(y)\n        if px == py:\n            return\n        if rank[px] < rank[py]:\n            parent[px] = py\n        elif rank[px] > rank[py]:\n            parent[py] = px\n        else:\n            parent[py] = px\n            rank[px] += 1\n    \n    # Special case: if any element is 1, it can't connect to anything (gcd(1, x) = 1)\n    for num in nums:\n        if num == 1:\n            return False\n    \n    # For each number, find its prime factors and connect indices that share prime factors\n    # Map prime factors to indices that contain them\n    prime_to_indices = defaultdict(list)\n    \n    for i, num in enumerate(nums):\n        # Get prime factors of num\n        temp = num\n        d = 2\n        while d * d <= temp:\n            if temp % d == 0:\n                prime_to_indices[d].append(i)\n                while temp % d == 0:\n                    temp //= d\n            d += 1\n        if temp > 1:\n            prime_to_indices[temp].append(i)\n    \n    # For each prime factor, connect all indices that have this prime factor\n    for prime, indices in prime_to_indices.items():\n        for i in range(1, len(indices)):\n            union(indices[0], indices[i])\n    \n    # Check if all indices belong to the same connected component\n    root = find(0)\n    for i in range(1, n):\n        if find(i) != root:\n            return False\n    \n    return True\n```",
