      "generated_answer": "The network structure is H → U ← P ← W, forming a \"V-structure\" where U is a child of both H and P, and P is a child of W.  \nWithout any independence assumptions, the number of independent parameters equals the sum over all variables of (number of states − 1) × (product of states of parents). Assuming binary variables (2 states each, standard unless stated), we get:  \n- H: 1 parameter (since no parents, 2−1 = 1)  \n- W: 1 parameter  \n- P: (2−1) × 2 = 2 parameters (1 parent, W, with 2 states)  \n- U: (2−1) × 2 × 2 = 4 parameters (2 parents, H and P, each with 2 states)  \nTotal = 1 + 1 + 2 + 4 = 8.  \n\n\\boxed{A}",
