    "prediction": "Qwen/Qwen3-Coder-Next",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The balanced budget multiplier equals one because when government spending and taxes increase by the same amount, the net effect on real GDP is equal to the increase in government spending (since the tax increase reduces consumption by less than the full amount due to the marginal propensity to consume being less than one). All other multipliers listed—such as the spending, investment, income, fiscal policy, and money multipliers—are generally greater than one (depending on parameters like MPC or reserve ratio), while multipliers like the AD or inflation multiplier are not standardly defined as equal to one. Elasticity of the long-run aggregate supply curve is zero (vertical curve), and interest rate and inflation multipliers are not standard concepts.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
